I think it's better if you phrase it
.i mi nelci lenu do dunda mi le mlatu
I like it that you gave me the cat

It makes much more sense than
.i mi lenu do dunda mi le mlatu kei cu nelci
I (you gave me the cat) like

I sounds a bit scrambled to the listener/reader. It is much easier on the
brain if you put the subject first ("I like" - the main purpose of the
sentence is to express your feelings (I think)). But to each his own ;-)

mi'e nei,omis.

